      "problem": "Given that the intersection of the elliptic cone $3(x+4)^{2}+8{y}^{2}=12{z}^{2}$ and the plane $z=-2$ is an ellipse, what is the length of its major axis?",
      "worked_solution": "To find the intersection of the elliptic cone and the plane $z=-2,$ we substitute $z=-2$ into the equation of the elliptic cone, and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3(x+4)^{2}+8{y}^{2} & =12{z}^{2} \\\\ 3(x+4)^{2}+8{y}^{2} & =12(-2)^{2} \\\\ 3(x+4)^{2}+8{y}^{2} & =48 \\\\ \\frac{(x+4)^{2}}{16}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{6} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x+4)^{2}}{{4}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{(\\sqrt{6})^{2}} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis gives us the equation of an ellipse with a semi-major axis of length $a=4.$ Therefore, the major axis has length $2a=8.$",
